# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: canonical patterns disambiguate by the rustc definitions, not by the translated items
#
# The `#0` of a canonical name pattern (`name#0` where a sibling has the same identifier) was decided
# from the names of the items a run translated: `CHARON_CALLGRAPH` looked at the translated items, and
# the `start_from_selected` patterns of the coverage report used no disambiguation at all. A run that
# selects `f::__Visitor#0` (serde's visitors and `__Field` enums in the arms of `visit_enum`, the
# statics of two expansions of a macro in one body) without its sibling `f::__Visitor#1` so printed
# `f::__Visitor`, which selects both: patterns did not round-trip between the whole-crate callgraph and
# the runs of its chunks.
#
# `TranslateCtx::name_disambiguation` now records the shared identifiers of the names Charon computed
# from the rustc definitions (`ExactResolver::shares_ident`: a definition named under the same parent
# has the same identifier with another disambiguator), whichever items are translated, and both the
# callgraph and the coverage report print canonical patterns with it (computed once, only if one of
# them is requested). `Pattern::canonical` takes the `Disambiguation`; `Disambiguation::new` (from
# names) and the undisambiguated `Pattern::canonical` are gone.

